# Cyclomatic complexity (Radon) — pydevops stricter deltas

Org floors and shared commands: **[`python-quality-gates.mdc`](python-quality-gates.mdc)**
(reads `docs/guardrails/python/profile.thresholds.yml`).

This repo is **stricter than the org floor** on gate code only (no deviation needed):

1. Run **`uv run --with radon python -m radon cc -s <each-edited-.py-file>`**.
2. **`scripts/quality_gates/**`**: every function you introduce or modify must be
   **grade A** on `radon cc -s` (extract helpers — do not leave grade B/C).
3. Other **`scripts/`** modules: keep complexity reasonable; refactor if radon
   reports **B** or higher on new/changed functions.

Malformed JSON often uses **booleans** where numbers are expected — **`bool`** is a
**`int`** subclass; use **`isinstance(x, (int, float)) and not isinstance(x, bool)`**
when reading numeric fields from artifacts.

See also **[`python-scripts-ci-gates.mdc`](python-scripts-ci-gates.mdc)** and
**[`interrogate-docstrings.mdc`](interrogate-docstrings.mdc)**.
